AID TOKEN CONTROLFLOW-TESTS
ATITLE CDATA Control Flow Tests
(SUITE
AID TOKEN IF-EXPRESSIONS
ATITLE CDATA If Expressions
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-If expressions evaluate a condition and return one of two values.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN IF-BASIC
ATITLE CDATA Basic If
(TESTS
(PROSE
-The if expression takes a boolean condition and two branches.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN IF-TRUE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM IMPLIED
(TEST
(INPUT
-if true : 1 else 2
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-1\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN IF-FALSE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM IMPLIED
(TEST
(INPUT
-if false : 1 else 2
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-2\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN IF-COMPARISON
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM IMPLIED
(TEST
(INPUT
-if 5 > 3 : 10 else 20
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN IF-WITH-BINDINGS
ATITLE CDATA If with Bindings
(TESTS
(PROSE
-If expressions can use values from let bindings.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN IF-WITH-LET
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-let x 5\nif x > 3 : x * 2 else x
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN IF-MAX
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-let a 7\nlet b 3\nif a > b : a else b
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-7\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN WHILE-LOOPS
ATITLE CDATA While Loops
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-While loops repeat as long as a condition is true.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN WHILE-BASIC
ATITLE CDATA Basic While
(TESTS
(PROSE
-A while loop evaluates its body repeatedly while the condition is true.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN WHILE-SIMPLE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 0\nwhile x < 3 : set x : x + 1\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-3\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN WHILE-ZERO-ITERATIONS
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 10\nwhile x < 5 : set x : x + 1\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN WHILE-ACCUMULATION
ATITLE CDATA While with Accumulation
(TESTS
(PROSE
-While loops can accumulate values across iterations.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN WHILE-SUM
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var sum 0\nvar i 1\nwhile i <= 3 : { set sum : sum + i: set i : i + 1 }\nsum
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-6\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN WHILE-FACTORIAL
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var result 1\nvar n 5\nwhile n > 0 : { set result : result * n: set n : n - 1 }\nresult
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-120\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN FOR-LOOPS
ATITLE CDATA For Loops
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-For loops iterate over a range of integers.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN FOR-BASIC
ATITLE CDATA Basic For
(TESTS
(PROSE
-A for loop iterates from 0 to n-1 where n is the range expression.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN FOR-COUNT
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var count 0\nfor i in 3 : set count : count + 1\ncount
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-3\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN FOR-ZERO-ITERATIONS
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 42\nfor i in 0 : set x : 0\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN FOR-ACCUMULATION
ATITLE CDATA For with Accumulation
(TESTS
(PROSE
-For loops can accumulate values using the loop variable.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN FOR-SUM
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var sum 0\nfor i in 5 : set sum : sum + i\nsum
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN FOR-FACTORIAL
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var prod 1\nfor i in 4 : set prod : prod * (i + 1)\nprod
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-24\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN BREAK-CONTINUE
ATITLE CDATA Break and Continue
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-Break exits a loop early, continue skips to the next iteration.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN BREAK-STATEMENTS
ATITLE CDATA Break Statements
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Break exits the innermost enclosing loop.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN BREAK-IN-FOR
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var sum 0\nfor i in 10 : { if i = 3 : break else set sum : sum + i }\nsum
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-3\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN BREAK-IN-WHILE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 0\nwhile x < 100 : { set x : x + 1: if x = 5 : break }\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-5\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN CONTINUE-STATEMENTS
ATITLE CDATA Continue Statements
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Continue skips the rest of the current iteration and continues with the next.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN CONTINUE-IN-FOR
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var sum 0\nfor i in 6 : { if i % 2 = 1 : continue else set sum : sum + i }\nsum
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-6\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN CONTINUE-IN-WHILE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var sum 0\nvar i 0\nwhile i < 10 : { let current i: set i : i + 1: if current % 2 = 1 : continue else set sum : sum + current }\nsum
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-20\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN NESTED-LOOPS
ATITLE CDATA Nested Loops
(TESTS
(PROSE
-By default break and continue affect only the innermost loop.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN BREAK-IN-NESTED
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var count 0\nfor i in 3 : { for j in 10 : { if j = 2 : break else set count : count + 1 } }\ncount
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-6\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN CONTINUE-IN-NESTED
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var count 0\nfor i in 3 : { for j in 5 : { if j % 2 = 1 : continue else set count : count + 1 } }\ncount
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-9\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN LABELED-LOOPS
ATITLE CDATA Labeled Break and Continue
(TESTS
(PROSE
-A loop may carry a label written `label NAME` after its colon.\n        From within a nested loop, `break loop NAME` exits the named loop and\n        `continue loop NAME` jumps to its next iteration, rather than acting on\n        the innermost loop.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN BREAK-LABELED-OUTER
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var count 0\nfor i in 3 : label outer { for j in 5 : { if j = 2 : break loop outer else set count : count + 1 } }\ncount
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-2\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN CONTINUE-LABELED-OUTER
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var count 0\nfor i in 3 : label outer { for j in 5 : { if j = 0 : continue loop outer else set count : count + 100 } }\ncount
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-0\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN REPEAT-LOOPS
ATITLE CDATA Repeat Loops
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-A repeat loop runs its body forever and exits only through break (or\n    return). Because break is the only way out, a break carrying a value\n    (`break v`) makes the repeat an expression that yields that value.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN REPEAT-BASIC
ATITLE CDATA Repeat and Break Value
(TESTS
(PROSE
-The value of a repeat expression is the operand of the break\n        that exits it.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN REPEAT-BREAK-VALUE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var i 0\nlet answer repeat { if i = 5 : break i + 100 else set i : i + 1 }\nanswer
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-105\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN REPEAT-COUNTER
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var i 0\nrepeat { if i = 3 : break else set i : i + 1 }\ni
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-3\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
AID TOKEN VAR-SET
ATITLE CDATA Mutable Variables
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-Mutable variables can be modified with set statements.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN VAR-BASIC
ATITLE CDATA Basic Var and Set
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Var creates a mutable variable, set modifies it.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN VAR-SIMPLE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 5\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-5\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN VAR-ASSIGN
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 5\nset x : 10\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN VAR-INCREMENT
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var x 3\nset x : x + 1\nx
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-4\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN VAR-MULTIPLE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-var a 2\nvar b 3\nset a : a * b\na
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-6\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
)SUITE
C
